3.—(1) Subject to sub-paragraph (3), an amount of $200 is to be paid to each non-schooling member of the following description:
(a)a member who is at least 7 years old and not older than 12 years old;
(b)a member —
(i)who is at least 13 years old but below 15 years old;
(ii)who is receiving home-schooling and is described in paragraph 3(1)(b) of the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order (Cap. 51, O 1); and
(iii)who, in the year 2013, has not performed, at the Primary School Leaving Examination and the National Education Quiz, at such level of educational achievement that the Director-General of Education may determine for that Examination and Quiz;
(c)a member who is —
(i)at least 13 years old and not older than 16 years old;
(ii)a pupil of a designated school within the meaning of paragraph 2 of the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order; and
(iii)receiving primary level education in the designated school.
(2) Subject to sub-paragraph (3), an amount of $240 is to be paid to each non-schooling member of the following description:
(a)a member who is —
(i)at least 13 years old and not older than 16 years old;
(ii)a pupil of a designated school within the meaning of paragraph 2 of the Compulsory Education (Exemption) Order; and
(iii)receiving secondary level education in the designated school;
(b)a member, other than a member referred to in sub-paragraph (1)(b) or (c), who is at least 13 years old and not older than 16 years old.
(3) No amount is to be paid to a non-schooling member who is 16 years old and who attains 17 years of age at any time in 2014.
